  "note": "Japanese follows the full playbook from the first pass. Two things are already visible in the source set and must be corrected before this cuisine is called done. FIRST, it skews hard to OMAKASE - five of the fourteen sources are omakase-only guides, because that is what publishers write about. Ramen, izakaya, katsu, udon and konbini-style counters are a different population and need their own subtype passes, exactly as pizza did inside Italian. SECOND, guide.michelin.com returns 403 to the fetcher (see the awards pass in research-playbook.json), so the awards leg is served by the Wikipedia star tables, which have the added benefit of carrying year-by-year history - a star is a claim with a date. Five sources 403'd or failed on the first fetch and were REMOVED rather than left in place - a dead source inflates the apparent breadth of the evidence without adding any. They were replaced with eleven subtype sources (ramen, izakaya, katsu, udon), which also corrects the omakase skew. Every URL came from a search result, never from a guessed path.",
